<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thrissur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Trichur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thrissur is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built around the Vadakkunnathan Temple on a hill at its centre. Rebuilt and enlarged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakthan-thampuran">Sakthan Thampuran</a>, ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kochi">Cochin</a> from 1790 to 1805, it became a commercial hub and is known as the cultural capital of Kerala. Its annual Thrissur Pooram temple festival draws huge crowds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thrissur.jpg" alt="Thrissur" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jpullokaran · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JJP_112.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
